---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
const questions = [{"prompt": "Wie viele Geschwister hat Johannes?", "options": ["zwei", "drei", "vier"], "answer": "drei", "why": "He has one brother and two sisters."}, {"prompt": "Wie heißt Johannes’ Vater?", "options": ["Sven", "Paul", "Dirk"], "answer": "Sven", "why": "His father is Sven; Paul is his brother."}, {"prompt": "Lea ist ___ Jahre alt.", "options": ["8", "13", "18"], "answer": "18", "why": "Lea is 18, Julia is 13 and Paul is 8."}, {"prompt": "Wo wohnen Julias Vater und Bruder?", "options": ["Stuttgart", "Hamburg", "Berlin"], "answer": "Hamburg", "why": "Both live in Hamburg."}, {"prompt": "Wie heißt Julias Bruder?", "options": ["Noah", "Niko", "Andreas"], "answer": "Noah", "why": "Noah is her brother; Niko is her cousin."}, {"prompt": "Andreas und Thomas haben ___ Kinder adoptiert.", "options": ["ein", "zwei", "drei"], "answer": "zwei", "why": "Their children are Niko and Anna."}, {"prompt": "Ihr ___ in Hamburg.", "options": ["wohnen", "wohnt", "wohnst"], "answer": "wohnt", "why": "With ihr, use wohnt."}, {"prompt": "Ich habe ___ Onkel.", "options": ["ein", "eine", "einen"], "answer": "einen", "why": "The masculine direct object takes einen."}];
---
<Base title="Lesson 3: Familie — families and connections" description="Meet Johannes and Julia, listen to their family stories, and practise describing family connections.">
<div class="lesson-two"><header class="lesson-hero"><div class="wrap">
<a class="back" href="/resources/german-async#e1">← Back to your learning path</a><p class="eyebrow">UNIT 01 · LESSON 03 · MAIN LESSON</p><h1>Families come<br /><em>in many forms.</em></h1><p class="intro">Meet Johannes and Julia. Learn to describe family connections, then practise with two videos.</p><p class="context">Start with the readings and audio, then watch, practise and speak. Continue to the <a href="/resources/german-lesson-3-extension">extension</a> for two different family stories and follow-up practice.</p><nav aria-label="Lesson steps"><a href="#read">01 Read &amp; listen</a><a href="#watch">02 Watch</a><a href="#practice">03 Practise</a><a href="#write">04 Write</a></nav></div></header>
<div class="wrap lesson-body"><section id="read" aria-labelledby="read-title"><p class="eyebrow">01 / READ &amp; LISTEN</p><h2 id="read-title">Two ways to describe family.</h2><p>Read each account for its main idea first. Then look for who belongs to each family and where they live.</p><article class="reading"><h3>Johannes</h3><p lang="de">Hallo! Mein Name ist Johannes. Ich bin 16 Jahre alt. Ich komme aus Stuttgart. Meine Familie ist sehr groß. Ich habe eine Mutter und einen Vater und drei Geschwister, einen Bruder und zwei Schwestern. Meine Mutter heißt Anja. Mein Vater heißt Sven. Eine Schwester ist älter als ich, und sie heißt Lea. Lea ist 18 Jahre alt. Meine andere Schwester, Julia, ist 13 Jahre alt. Paul, mein Bruder, ist erst 8 Jahre alt.</p><audio controls preload="none" src="/assets/german/lesson3/johannes.mp4" aria-label="Johannes describes family"></audio><a class="small" href="/assets/german/lesson3/johannes.mp4" download>Download Johannes’s audio</a></article><article class="reading"><h3>Julia</h3><p lang="de">Guten Tag, ich heiße Julia und komme aus Hamburg. Ich bin 28 Jahre alt. In meiner Familie habe ich einen Vater und einen Bruder. Sie wohnen beide in Hamburg. Mein Bruder heißt Noah und er ist 25 Jahre alt. Mein Vater, Dirk, hat auch einen Bruder, der Andreas heißt, und eine Schwester, Monika. Onkel Andreas hat einen Partner, Thomas, und sie haben zwei Kinder adoptiert, Niko und Anna. Niko ist mein Cousin und Anna ist meine Cousine. Tante Monika ist verheiratet. Ihr Mann heißt Markus.</p><audio controls preload="none" src="/assets/german/lesson3/julia.mp4" aria-label="Julia describes family"></audio><a class="small" href="/assets/german/lesson3/julia.mp4" download>Download Julia’s audio</a></article></section>
<section id="watch" aria-labelledby="watch-title"><p class="eyebrow">02 / LISTENING PRACTICE</p><h2 id="watch-title">Meet more families.</h2><h3 class="subheading">Sarah und Daniele</h3><p>Listen for family words. What do Großvater / Opa, Großmutter / Oma and Großeltern mean?</p><div class="video"><iframe title="Sarah und Daniele: family listening activity" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/288167686?h=9205d6ffa2" width="640" height="360" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe></div><p class="small">Internet required. <a href="https://player.vimeo.com/video/288167686?h=9205d6ffa2">Open this video separately</a>.</p><h3 class="subheading">Karl, Laura und Tiradard</h3><p>Choose one speaker and sketch their family tree. Listen again to check it, then introduce that family in your own words.</p><div class="video"><iframe title="Karl, Laura und Tiradard: family listening activity" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/288168172?h=7d1f35d549" width="640" height="360" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe></div><p class="small">Internet required. <a href="https://player.vimeo.com/video/288168172?h=7d1f35d549">Open this video separately</a>.</p></section><section id="practice" aria-labelledby="practice-title"><p class="eyebrow">03 / CHECK &amp; APPLY</p><h2 id="practice-title">People, verbs and connections.</h2><div class="grammar-grid"><article><h3>Talking about more than one person</h3><ul><li><span lang="de">wir haben / wir wohnen</span> — we have / live</li><li><span lang="de">ihr habt / ihr wohnt</span> — you have / live (informal plural)</li><li><span lang="de">sie haben / sie wohnen</span> — they have / live</li><li><span lang="de">Sie haben / Sie wohnen</span> — you have / live (formal)</li></ul><p>Use <span lang="de">du</span> for one person informally, <span lang="de">ihr</span> for several informally, and <span lang="de">Sie</span> for formal address. Context and the verb help distinguish <span lang="de">sie</span> (she) from <span lang="de">sie</span> (they).</p></article><article><h3>The person or thing you have</h3><p>After <span lang="de">haben</span>, the direct object is in the accusative. Masculine articles change; the other forms shown here stay the same.</p><ul lang="de"><li>ein Bruder → Ich habe <strong>einen Bruder</strong>.</li><li>eine Schwester → Ich habe <strong>eine Schwester</strong>.</li><li>ein Kind → Ich habe <strong>ein Kind</strong>.</li></ul></article></div><p class="tip">For regular verbs such as <span lang="de">wohnen</span>, start with the stem <span lang="de">wohn-</span>: <span lang="de">ich wohne, du wohnst, er/sie/es wohnt, wir wohnen, ihr wohnt, sie/Sie wohnen</span>. Compare <span lang="de">du arbeitest</span> (an extra e) and <span lang="de">du heißt</span> (no extra s).</p><p>Answer from the readings and grammar notes. Check your answers, read the feedback, and try again.</p>
 <form id="lesson-quiz">{questions.map((q,i)=><fieldset data-answer={q.answer} data-explanation={q.why}><legend><span>{String(i+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span> <span lang="de">{q.prompt}</span></legend><div class="choices">{q.options.map(option=><label><input type="radio" name={`q${i}`} value={option}/><span lang="de">{option}</span></label>)}</div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset>)}<div class="quiz-actions"><button type="submit">Check my answers</button><button type="reset" class="secondary">Try again</button></div><p id="quiz-score" role="status"></p></form>
 <noscript><p>Interactive checking needs JavaScript. Answer key: {questions.map((q,i)=>`${i+1}. ${q.answer}`).join(' · ')}.</p></noscript>
</section><section id="write" aria-labelledby="write-title"><p class="eyebrow">04 / MAKE IT YOURS</p><h2 id="write-title">Describe a family.</h2><ol class="speaking"><li>Write two sentences about Johannes’ or Julia’s family using <span lang="de">haben</span> and <span lang="de">wohnen</span>.</li><li>Describe your own family, chosen family, or an invented family in four sentences. Mention people, connections and where they live.</li><li>Underline your verbs and check that they match the subject. Check <span lang="de">ein / eine / einen</span> after <span lang="de">haben</span>.</li></ol><p class="example" lang="de">Wir wohnen in Berlin. Ich habe einen Bruder und eine Schwester.</p><p>Useful words: <span lang="de">die Eltern</span> (parents), <span lang="de">die Geschwister</span> (siblings), <span lang="de">die Großeltern</span> (grandparents), <span lang="de">die Nichte</span> (niece), <span lang="de">der Neffe</span> (nephew), <span lang="de">befreundet</span> (friends with one another), <span lang="de">verheiratet</span> (married).</p><a class="next" href="/resources/german-lesson-3-extension">Next: extension practice →</a></section>
<aside class="source"><h2>Source &amp; adaptation</h2><p>Adapted from <a href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/e1/l3/">Grenzenlos Deutsch, Lektion 3: Familie</a>, supplied as a saved-page ZIP, under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/">CC BY-NC-SA 4.0</a>. Reading texts are reproduced from the archive. Johannes and Julia audio files and both Vimeo embeds were supplied separately. Explanations and tasks are adapted; eight text-based questions replace the original embedded exercises. Interactive family trees and original embedded exercises are not reproduced. Vimeo requires internet and remains subject to the video owners’ rights. This page has no offline-saving feature.</p><p>Original funding: National Endowment for the Humanities and the Mansergh-Stuessy Fund for College Innovation. Ramzunā Languages is not affiliated with the original authors.</p></aside></div></div></Base>
<script>
const quiz = document.querySelector<HTMLFormElement>('#lesson-quiz');
quiz?.addEventListener('submit',event=>{event.preventDefault();let score=0;const fields=quiz.querySelectorAll<HTMLFieldSetElement>('fieldset');fields.forEach(field=>{const selected=field.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('input:checked');const correct=selected?.value===field.dataset.answer;if(correct)score++;const feedback=field.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.feedback')!;feedback.textContent=!selected?'Choose an answer first.':`${correct?'Correct.':'Not quite.'} ${field.dataset.explanation}`;field.dataset.result=!selected?'empty':correct?'correct':'incorrect';});document.querySelector('#quiz-score')!.textContent=`${score} of ${fields.length} correct. Review the feedback above and try again whenever you like.`;});
quiz?.addEventListener('reset',()=>{quiz.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.feedback').forEach(el=>el.textContent='');quiz.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('fieldset').forEach(el=>delete el.dataset.result);document.querySelector('#quiz-score')!.textContent='';});
</script>
